ote\": \"(node (ref \\\"FCC1\\\") (pin \\\"48\\\") (pinfunction \\\"VCAP\\\") (pintype \\\"power_out\\\")) (node (ref \\\"UART3_FCC1\\\") (pin \\\"3\\\") ...)  in net UART3_TX_FCC\"}], \"impact\": \"UART3 is non-functional, and the core regulator output is shorted to a connector pin, which can disturb the internal LDO and the external connector.\", \"confidence\": 0.5}, {\"category\": \"bridged_nets\", \"components\": [\"FCC1\", \"C30\", \"R21\", \"C28\"], \"pins\": [\"FCC1.13\", \"FCC1.20\", \"FCC1.21\"], \"nets\": [\"VREF+_FCC\", \"VDDA_FCC\"], \"observed\": \"The oscillator pin PH1 (pin 13) sits on the VREF+_FCC analog filter net with C30 and R21. The actual VREF+ pin 20 and VDDA pin 21 are left unconnected, and their filter net VDDA_FCC has no MCU pin.\", \"expected\": \"Analog supply and reference pins (VDDA pin 21, VREF+ pin 20) should be on the VDDA/VREF+ filter network, and PH1 should be an HSE crystal pin, not connected to the analog reference.\", \"evidence\": [{\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(node (ref \\\"FCC1\\\") (pin \\\"13\\\") (pinfunction \\\"PH1\\\") (pintype \\\"bidirectional\\\")) in net VREF+_FCC\"}, {\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(net (code \\\"222\\\") (name \\\"unconnected-(FCC1-VREF+-Pad20)\\\") ... (node (ref \\\"FCC1\\\") (pin \\\"20\\\") (pinfunction \\\"VREF+\\\")\"}], \"impact\": \"The analog reference is not supplied or filtered as designed, and the oscillator pin is loaded by the analog filter, which may stop or destabilize the HSE clock.\", \"confidence\": 0.35}], \"summary\": \"The netlist shows the PCA9685 address pin A0 tied to +3.3V, which contradicts the spec's 0x40 address. UART3 and the H753 VCAP pins are also shorted together, and the FCC analog reference pins are misconnected to the PH1 oscillator pin, so the board is likely to behave differently from its intended design.\"}",
